  "text": "You are an expert multimodal affective understanding assistant.\nTreat the original video, audio and text as primary evidence. AMG evidence is auxiliary and must be verified against the original input.\nCue scores are source-domain calibrated detector scores, not emotion probabilities or target-domain guarantees.\nCA (Cue to Appraisal) and CE (Cue to Emotion) are signed conditional predictive associations, not causal relations. Sample contributions are logit terms, not probabilities.\nTreat Appraisal and Emotion nodes as hypotheses. The two branches are parallel; do not assume Appraisal causes Emotion.\nUse unrestricted natural-language emotion vocabulary. Answer the user's actual question.\n\n[AMG EVIDENCE — AUXILIARY]\nCue scores (source-domain calibrated detector scores):\n- [Text] TXT_NEGATION_PRESENT | score=1.00 | Semantically functioning negation; contrast and uncertainty alone do not qualify.\n- [Visual] VIS_BROWS_FURROWED | score=0.99 | Visible inward brow contraction or furrowing; low brow position alone is insufficient.\n- [Text] TXT_CONTRAST_PRESENT | score=0.99 | Explicit contrast or reversal construction.\n- [Visual] VIS_MOUTH_CORNERS_DOWN | score=0.99 | Clearly downward mouth corners, distinct from speaking or perspective effects.\n- [Audio] AUD_SPEECH_RATE_REL_SLOW | score=0.98 | Slower speech relative to comparable segments from the same speaker.\n- [Audio] AUD_INTONATION_FALLING | score=0.93 | Clearly falling acoustic intonation.\n- [Audio] AUD_PITCH_VARIABILITY_LOW | score=0.78 | Clearly limited pitch variation across the observed speech.\n- [Visual] VIS_GRIMACE_PRESENT | score=0.71 | Directly visible facial grimacing or distortion.\n\nCE: Cue → Emotion\n- Hypothesis: disappointed\n  - AUD_INTONATION_FALLING: C=+0.5981\n  - TXT_NEGATION_PRESENT: C=+0.5757\n  - AUD_PITCH_VARIABILITY_LOW: C=-0.3149\n  - VIS_MOUTH_CORNERS_DOWN: C=+0.3144\n  - TXT_CONTRAST_PRESENT: C=+0.2682\n  - VIS_GRIMACE_PRESENT: C=+0.1258\n  - AUD_SPEECH_RATE_REL_SLOW: C=+0.1208\n\n[END OF AMG EVIDENCE]",
